h3 "Navbar menu #" @17,7566,694,19
text The navbar-menu is the counterpart of the navbar brand. As such, it must appear as a direct child of navbar, as a sibling of navbar-brand. @17,7597,694,41
card @17,7650,694,139
  text <nav class="navbar" role="navigation" aria-label="main navigation"> <div class="navbar-brand"> <!-- navbar items, navbar burger... --> </div> <div class="navbar-menu"> <!-- navbar start, navbar end --> </div> </nav> @34,7665,660,61
  button Copy success @34,7738,660,36
text The navbar-menu is hidden on touch devices < 1024px . You need to add the modifier class is-active to display it. @17,7801,694,41
card @17,7854,694,118
  text <div class="navbar-menu"> <!-- hidden on mobile --> </div> <div class="navbar-menu is-active"> <!-- shown on mobile --> </div> @34,7869,660,40
  button Copy success @34,7921,660,36
text On desktop 1024px , the navbar-menu will fill up the space available in the navbar, leaving the navbar brand just the space it needs. It needs, however, two elements as direct children: @17,7984,694,41
